      "body": "Hi @mzumsande, @fjahr, and @l0rinc, could you take a look ?\r\n\r\nSince the locator change in #34897, a flush can report a block before the index receives BlockConnected for it. Would you prefer letting the index save its current tip when the flushed block is ahead on the same chain, or changing the callback order in validation?",
