      "body": "@LakshyaBagani I already developed a fix, just didn't get around to open the PR yet. You can see the branch here: https://github.com/fjahr/bitcoin/commits/2026-11-index-flush-commit/ I think that approach is better because `Commit()` already refuses to write unless the index's best block is an ancestor of the chainstate's last flushed block, so the locator check that you keep and even widen here can only block commits that are safe, and removing it leaves one rule in one place. If you want you maintain it you can pull my commits in here, otherwise I can open a separate PR.",
